  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/langs1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 9ae4abe13f. _extract_param_types (py.py:4428, local_symbols checked before imports at ~4452) is unchanged. Fixture fx_masov: pkg/m.py defines class Foo, then 'from pkg.other import Foo', then def use(x: Foo): x.bar(). Survey emits a RESOLVED calls edge use -> python:pkg/m.py:2-3:Foo.bar:method at confidence 0.85 (evidence_derived, ast_call); the right target is pkg/other.py Foo.bar. So the residual is not just imprecision: a confidently-wrong direct-method edge is live, the 'surface elsewhere' case the item predicted. The low-priority rationale ('the confidently-wrong edge is already closed') is false. MECHANISM: bare-annotation lookup checks local_symbols before imports, ignoring Python last-binding-wins, so var_types holds the shadowed local class. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-dagig."  # ff2e
