    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 9ae4abe13f. _extract_param_types (py.py:4428, local_symbols checked before imports at ~4452) is unchanged. Fixture fx_masov: pkg/m.py defines class Foo, then 'from pkg.other import Foo', then def use(x: Foo): x.bar(). Survey emits a RESOLVED calls edge use -> python:pkg/m.py:2-3:Foo.bar:method at confidence 0.85 (evidence_derived, ast_call); the right target is pkg/other.py Foo.bar. So the residual is not just imprecision: a confidently-wrong direct-method edge is live, the 'surface elsewhere' case the item predicted. The low-priority rationale ('the confidently-wrong edge is already closed') is false. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nDeeper root cause behind the WI-supat PR-A adversarial-review blocker. When resolving a bare `param: Name` annotation, `_extract_param_types` (py.py ~3565) deterministically prefers `local_symbols.get(type_name)` (a LOCAL class) over a same-named import, even when the import SHADOWS the local class (Python last-binding-wins: `class Foo(...)` followed by `from x import Foo` rebinds `Foo` to the import). So `var_types[param]` holds the WRONG class in that self-shadow case.\n\nWI-supat PR-A closed the CONFIDENTLY-WRONG downstream symptom at the producer (the `_receiver_type_id_trustworthy` gate omits `receiver_type_id` when the resolved type is the in-file class AND the name is import-shadowed, so no wrong resolved edge is minted). But the underlying var_types mis-resolution remains and could surface elsewhere (e.g. Case 2c/2f direct method resolution on the wrong local type, or any future consumer of var_types).\n\nFix options: (a) when a bare annotation name is BOTH a local class and an import, bias `_extract_param_types` to unresolved (drop the entry); or (b) honor Python import precedence (last binding wins) — resolve to the import. (a) is the conservative INV-fahub-aligned choice. Low priority: the confidently-wrong edge is already closed by WI-supat PR-A; this is the residual imprecision, and the trigger (F811 self-shadow: a local class def immediately shadowed by a same-name import in one module) is pathological."  # fe8d
